            <ul id="what-card-container">

                <li class="what-card" id="card-1-container">
                    <div class="card-img" id="card-1"></div>
                    <div class="card-content">
                         <h3>Regulatory Strategy for Advanced Biotechnologies</h3>
                        <p>Advanced therapies rarely follow a conventional development path. We help emerging biotechnology companies build regulatory strategies around the product’s science, manufacturing platform, clinical objectives, and business milestones.</p>

                        <p>Our team supports tissue-based products, peptides, large molecules, biologics, and drug-device combination products from early development through marketing applications. We prepare sponsors for FDA interactions, develop briefing packages, provide meeting representation, and help resolve complex scientific and procedural issues.</p>

                        <p>Where appropriate, we also evaluate opportunities for earlier or more intensive FDA engagement through programs such as INTERACT meetings, Fast Track, Breakthrough Therapy, Regenerative Medicine Advanced Therapy designation, and the START Pilot Program for qualifying rare-disease therapies. Our focus is not simply obtaining a designation—it is using the most appropriate regulatory mechanism to reduce uncertainty and advance a credible development program.</p>


