                        <h3>Integrated Product Manufacturing, and Quality Expertise</h3>
                        <p>For biotechnology companies, regulatory strategy and manufacturing strategy are inseparable. We bring practical experience with Good Manufacturing Practice, Good Laboratory Practice, and Good Documentation Practice requirements to help clients anticipate the quality and CMC issues that can delay development or undermine regulatory submissions.</p>

                        <p>We support regulatory planning for innovative manufacturing platforms, comparability strategies, analytical methods, process changes, technology transfers, and the transition from clinical to commercial production.</p>

                        <p>When a technology may qualify, we help clients assess engagement opportunities through FDA initiatives such as CDER’s Emerging Technology Program, CBER’s Advanced Technologies Team, and the Advanced Manufacturing Technologies Designation Program. These pathways can provide valuable early dialogue with FDA regarding novel manufacturing methods, controls, and implementation strategies.</p>

                        <h4>Procurement Services:</h4>
                        <p>Buying the correct excipients.  Let us explain why this matters for your IND and NDA submission but also for global submissions.   This is often a matter that is overlooked but directly affects your product’s value.    </p>
